    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351-a3">

                <pb facs="0479" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg395"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr.
                            Galvan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santo Domingo City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your
                    excellency’s note of October 22, 1903, conveying to me the kindly expressions
                    from His Excellency General Woss y Gil, President of this Republic, in response
                    to a congratulatory letter from Mr. Roosevelt, the President of the United
                    States of America.</p>
                <pb facs="0480" n="396" xml:id="pg396"/>
                <p>It will afford me great pleasure to communicate the contents of your excellency’s
                    very interesting letter to my Government.</p>
                <p>Allow me to express to your excellency the great pleasure that Mr. Roosevelt, the
                    President, will feel in reading the kindly sentiments that His Excellency the
                    President, General Woss y Gil, and his cabinet have for the Government and
                    people of the United States.</p>
                <p>I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
